# [Project Name]

## Agents

This project uses Claude Code and Codex with the global rules and skills from the agent configuration repo. Project-specific rules in this file override global defaults when they conflict.

Project facts come from `AGENTS.md`, ordinary docs, and agent-run. Use `agent-run detect --json` to preview likely commands, `agent-run detect --add <name>` (repeatable) or `agent-run detect --all` to register them, `agent-run list --json` to inspect registrations, and `agent-run run <name> --json` or `agent-run run --json -- <argv>` to run commands. Agent-run keeps output bounded and full logs; manual-only commands and raw Playwright/Cypress are blocked by the guard. Setup checks that these global commands are installed: `project-checks-repo-context`, `project-checks-change-impact`, `project-checks-generated-file-guard`, and `project-checks-markdown-claims`. Current work belongs in `PROGRESS.md` at the project root when a multi-session plan is active.

